# ---- Secrets & credentials ----
# No credential belongs in this repository in any form. Terraform generates the
# only one into Secret Manager; the Kubernetes Secret is created from it at
# deploy time. These patterns are a backstop against a stray hand-made file.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!terraform.tfvars.example
*-sa.json
*-key.json
credentials.json
gcp-*.json
service-account*.json
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.p12
kubeconfig*
.kube/
backend.hcl

# No secrets directory exists: Terraform generates the only credential into
# Secret Manager, so nothing needs encrypting-and-committing. These patterns
# remain as a backstop against a stray hand-made file.
secrets/
*secret*.yaml
*credentials*.yaml

# ---- Terraform ----
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl.bak
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
tfplan
tfdestroy
crash.log
crash.*.log
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# NOTE: .terraform.lock.hcl IS committed on purpose (provider pinning).

# ---- Build / app ----
node_modules/
dist/
build/
*.log

# ---- Attribution, not secrets ----
# wizexercise.txt carries a real person's name. That is not a secret (it is on
# the CV that accompanies this exercise) so encrypting it would be theatre —
# but it also has no reason to sit in a public repository or its history.
# `just build` generates it from WIZ_EXERCISE_NAME immediately before the
# docker build, so the IMAGE always carries the real name while the REPO never
# does. See app/wizexercise.txt.example.
app/wizexercise.txt

# ---- Slidev ----
.slidev/
slides/*.pdf
slides/png-out/
slides/shot-*.png

# Generated by `just slides` from slides/parts/, with the presenter's name
# substituted in. Same reasoning as app/wizexercise.txt above: the rendered
# deck carries the name, the repository does not.
slides/slides.md

# ---- Generated, and environment-identifying ----
# Written by scripts/setup-lab.sh. Records the operator's PUBLIC IP, the GCP
# organisation ID and the project number — none of them secret, but a home IP
# address is geolocatable and has no business in a public repository. It is
# regenerated on every setup run, so redacting it in place would not hold.
# The only durable facts it carries (the capability-probe results) are recorded
# in docs/decisions.md instead.
docs/lab-environment.md

# ---- OS / editor ----
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# direnv local overrides
.envrc.local
